From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 07:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: mp01: Use the vendor DSI link timing

The e-paper controller decodes the DSI link only with the vendor kernel's
blanking and lane timings: with them the picture is live and clean, with
mainline's it is garbled or streaked (seen on the phone).

Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6789-minimal-mp01.dts | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6789-minimal-mp01.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6789-minimal-mp01.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6789-minimal-mp01.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6789-minimal-mp01.dts
@@ -988,6 +988,8 @@
  * board (the vendor's lane_swap table).
  */
 &dsi0 {
+	/* The e-paper controller decodes only the vendor kernel's link timing. */
+	mediatek,vendor-link-timing;
 	status = "okay";
 
 	port {
-- 
2.47.0
